    "summary": "I built a single-cell storage box with a magnetic lid. It's one full hex base with a full-depth bin inside, a full cover on top as the lid, and solid end caps on all six sides. When I tried to turn the lid magnets on, the configurator said that changed nothing, which means they were already on. The parts list confirms it: 6 Ø5×1 mm neodymium disc magnets and 6 copper-coated 4.5 mm steel BBs. check_build passed with no issues, and the collision check came back clear. It's 12 parts, about 629 g of filament and roughly 857 minutes of printing. I didn't add props, since the brief is just the box.",
